 — Razor view for external auth buttons\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/ExtendedApplicationUser.cs` — Custom member fields with MapFromMemberInfo/MapToMemberInfo\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/MemberListExtender.cs` — PageExtender adding custom column to admin\n- `src/_code/src/CodeSamples/Membership/StandaloneSamples/MemberRetrievalExample.cs` — Member retrieval via UserManager\n\n### Documentation pages modified (4 files):\n- `registration-and-authentication.md` — Replaced inline blocks with code_link tags\n- `forms-authentication.md` — Replaced ~10 inline blocks with code_link tags\n- `external-authentication.md` — Replaced ~3 inline blocks with code_link tags\n- `add-fields-to-member-objects.md` — Replaced 2 inline blocks, fixed ApplicationUserManager → UserManager\n\n### API discrepancies fixed:\n- `ApplicationUserManager<TUser>` → `UserManager<TUser>` (2 occurrences — class does not exist in Xperience source)\n\n## What Remains and Why\nNothing — all phases completed successfully.\n\n## Key Decisions Made\n1. **Reused existing AccountController.cs** with selective `//Include:` markers to hide `ShoppingCartService` coupling — avoids duplicating working sign-in/register logic\n2. **Integrated password reset and email confirmation** into the webapp flow (not standalone) — these are core features any Xperience app would use\n3. **Kept external auth as standalone** — requires external provider config (Google, etc.) that shouldn't be baked into the shared webapp\n4. **Small Program.cs config snippets** (2-5 lines) left inline in docs — extracting adds complexity without value\n5. **Used `Codesamples.Membership.Standalone` namespace** for standalone samples — matches existing `Codesamples.Commerce.Standalone` convention\n6. **Supersedes DOC-3186 approach** (PR #3033) which put everything in StandaloneSamples — this task integrates compilable samples into the webapp with proper MVC structure\n\n## Source Code References\n- Claim: \"`ApplicationUserManager<TUser>` does not exist\" → Verified by researcher — standard `UserManager<T>` from Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity is used instead. [ApplicationUser.cs](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/ApplicationUser.cs)\n- Claim: \"`MapFromMemberInfo`/`MapToMemberInfo` are virtual methods\" → [ApplicationUser.cs](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/ApplicationUser.cs) — virtual methods available for override\n- Claim: \"`PageExtender<MemberList>` uses composition\" → [MemberList](https://app-xbyk-source-prod.azurewebsites.net/#Kentico.Membership/MemberList.cs) is sealed but PageExtender works via composition pattern\n\n## Review Status\nAll three reviewers approved on first pass (no revision cycles needed):\n- **Technical accuracy**: Approved — all API types, markers, and behavioral claims verified correct\n- **Style & grammar**: Approved — 3 non-blocking suggestions for minor consistency improvements\n- **Information architecture**: Approved — code sample migration preserves navigation, cross-references, and content flow\n\n## Open Questions Requiring Human Judgment\n- The 3 non-blocking style suggestions from the style reviewer may warrant minor tweaks at the reviewer's discretion\n- Verify rendered output of code_link tags on the 4 doc pages matches the original inline code blocks\n\n## Pull Request\n[PR #3034](https://dev.azure.com/KenticoCustomerSuccess/CustomerEducation/_git/kentico-docs-jekyll/pullrequest/3034) (draft)\n\n## Suggested Next Steps\n1. Review the PR diff — 20 files changed (9 new, 11 modified)\n2. Spot-check rendered code_link output on a few doc pages\n3. Confirm the Include marker regions in AccountController.cs correctly exclude ShoppingCartService references\n4. Merge when satisfied\n",
